 the Espionage only-list at +5. Language: Other is a Technical row and is reached through the Communications only-list; Technical''s +10% therefore does not apply to it. Lore skills: the Technical Lore rows filed for Rifts, without regional histories outside North America (Russia, China, Aborigines, Dreamtime). The Medical +10% is read as applying to both First Aid and Holistic Medicine. Dead Ball is the catalog row W.P. Deadball. SECONDARY: three plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. || SHAMAN: one in ten. A variant cannot carry magic, so the Shaman is a chosen special ability carrying the magic block (seven spells by name, one per level from level 2, Invocations levels 1-4); type spell, as the catalog''s mystic. The Shaman''s loss of W.P. Archery and Targeting, no extra W.P.s and halved secondary skills cannot be stated by an ability: prose in its description and the skill notes. || NATURAL ABILITIES: climb 92/82%, acrobats 90% and swimmers 65% are fixed racial figures, kept as ability text rather than skill rows (the dragon-cat precedent). || EQUIPMENT: small woven grass satchel or a satchel, backpack or shoulder bag stored as a choice of knapsack or backpack; crude wooden cross as wooden-cross; a bow as a choice of the Rifts short or long bow. Walking stick, club and arrows have no Rifts-system catalog row (club-stick-pipe and the arrow rows are Palladium Fantasy) and are a restriction line, as are the antler weapons (2D6 S.D.C.) and the bone-and-skin armor (20+2D6 M.D. main body). || MONEY: a player character has 1D6x1,000 credits worth of tradable goods, stored as starting_money 1d6x1000; most tribesmen have 1D6x100 in stones, in a restriction line. || NOT STORED: also known as Deep Forest Apes and Spinning Head Wildmen; size 4 feet, weight 90-100 pounds, life span 4D6+35, reproduction, pack size 2D6+5 (rarely 3D6+10), slave market value 1D4x1,000 (half to a freak show), habitat, allies and enemies are in GM Notes. Experience Level 1D4+1 for NPCs is a population figure."
