## Lore

In the superstition-soaked Dark Woods of Alabama, travelers tell of the
"Deep Forest Ape-Man": a hairless, gray-green apish D-Bee with an
alligator-like head, huge saucer eyes full of madness, and a neck that turns
like an owl''s, far enough to look straight behind or to hang the face upside
down. The tales are true. The creatures call themselves the Deer Horn Tribe,
after the antlers they worship and carve into weapons, tools and ornaments.

They are anything but orderly. Deer Horn packs are wild, rowdy and lewd,
delighting in shocking and scaring anyone they meet: dancing with corpses,
pelting travelers with mud, stealing, vandalizing, kidnapping and playing
cruel games of keep-away. Each pack is ruled by its strongest male, the
Chieftain, while the rest squabble endlessly over their place beneath him.
For all the bluster they are sycophants at heart, submissive to anyone
truly powerful.

One Deer Horn in ten is a Shaman, who knows a little magic by instinct.

A Deer Horn in a party of adventurers is hard work. Played in character it
can be enormous fun, but the player should take care not to torment the
rest of the group; at best the tribesman behaves like a boisterous child
given to pranks and theft.

## GM Notes

Starting money: the book prints 1D6x1,000 credits worth of tradable goods, not coin, so no starting_money is stored (money is coin only).

Also known as Deep Forest Apes and Spinning Head Wildmen. Size 4 feet (1.2
m); weight 90-100 pounds (40.5 to 45 kg). Life span 4D6+35 years; mature at
14; litters of 1D4 after a 10 month gestation, up to age 35.

Packs of 2D6+5, rarely as large as 3D6+10, almost entirely in the Dark Woods
of Alabama and parts of Mississippi; believed to have come through a Rift near
pre-Cataclysm Talladega.

Slave market value: none, except as a wild man in a freak show or zoo, or as
a crazy gladiator in Atlantis, where one may fetch up to 1D4x1,000 (half that
to a freak show).

Allies: their own kind, and even then they squabble between packs. Enemies:
they try to dominate or drive off every other intelligent being, but have
learned to avoid Splugorth Slavers, Horune Pirates and Forest Wardens.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'deer-horn-tribesman');


